    "##### Processing Planck data\n",
    "\n",
    "For the 143 GHz Planck maps, the physical beam scale is a property of the input data product and is distinct from the later flat-patch sampling. In this notebook we treat the 143 GHz half-rings as having an effective input beam of about 7.27 arcmin FWHM, then harmonically smooth to a common 10 arcmin FWHM resolution and downgrade to Nside = 512. The later 6.7 arcmin figure used in the flat-sky cells refers instead to the gnomonic patch pixel size, not to the Planck beam."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "659864ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "% Resolution change + Gaussian beam smoothing (HEALPix / Planck-style)\n",
    "\n",
    "1.  Harmonic representation.\n",
    "A scalar sky map (e.g.\\ temperature) can be expanded as\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "T(\\hat n)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{\\infty}\\sum_{m=-\\ell}^{\\ell} a_{\\ell m}^{T}\\,Y_{\\ell m}(\\hat n).\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "A HEALPix map at resolution $N_{\\rm side}$ is effectively band-limited to\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\ell_{\\max}\\ \\lesssim\\ 3N_{\\rm side}-1\n",
    "\\qquad(\\text{often one uses a more conservative }\\ell_{\\max}\\lesssim 2N_{\\rm side}).\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Resolution downgrade in harmonic space.\n",
    "Given a high-resolution map $T_{\\rm in}$, compute harmonic coefficients\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "a_{\\ell m}^{T,{\\rm in}}=\\int T_{\\rm in}(\\hat n)\\,Y_{\\ell m}^*(\\hat n)\\,d\\Omega.\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "To produce a lower-resolution map at $N_{\\rm side}^{\\rm out}$, choose an output bandlimit\n",
    "$\\ell_{\\max}^{\\rm out}$ compatible with $N_{\\rm side}^{\\rm out}$ and truncate:\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "a_{\\ell m}^{T,{\\rm out}}=\n",
    "\\begin{cases}\n",
    "a_{\\ell m}^{T,{\\rm in}}, & \\ell\\le \\ell_{\\max}^{\\rm out},\\\\\n",
    "0, & \\ell> \\ell_{\\max}^{\\rm out}.\n",
    "\\end{cases}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "Then synthesize on the coarser grid:\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "T_{\\rm out}(\\hat n)=\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{\\ell_{\\max}^{\\rm out}}\\sum_{m=-\\ell}^{\\ell}\n",
    "a_{\\ell m}^{T,{\\rm out}}\\,Y_{\\ell m}(\\hat n),\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "sampled at the $N_{\\rm side}^{\\rm out}$ pixel centers.\n",
    "This ``low-$\\ell$ projection + resampling'' avoids aliasing of high-$\\ell$ power.\n",
    "\n",
    "3.  Polarization and the $E/B$ decomposition.\n",
    "Polarization is a spin-2 field:\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "(Q\\pm iU)(\\hat n)=\\sum_{\\ell m} a_{\\ell m}^{\\pm2}\\,{}_{\\pm2}Y_{\\ell m}(\\hat n),\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "with $E/B$-mode coefficients defined by\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "a_{\\ell m}^{E}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\left(a_{\\ell m}^{2}+a_{\\ell m}^{-2}\\right),\\qquad\n",
    "a_{\\ell m}^{B}=\\frac{i}{2}\\left(a_{\\ell m}^{2}-a_{\\ell m}^{-2}\\right).\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "In practice one transforms $(T,Q,U)\\mapsto (a_{\\ell m}^T,a_{\\ell m}^E,a_{\\ell m}^B)$,\n",
    "applies bandlimiting/smoothing to $T,E,B$, then transforms back to $(T,Q,U)$.\n",
    "\n",
    "4.  Beam smoothing in harmonic space.\n",
    "For a rotationally symmetric beam, convolution is multiplicative in harmonic space:\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "a_{\\ell m}^{X,{\\rm obs}} = B_\\ell\\,a_{\\ell m}^{X,{\\rm true}},\n",
    "\\qquad X\\in\\{T,E,B\\}.\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "For a Gaussian beam of FWHM $\\theta_{\\rm FWHM}$ (in radians),\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "B_\\ell=\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{\\ell(\\ell+1)\\sigma_b^2}{2}\\right),\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "\\sigma_b=\\frac{\\theta_{\\rm FWHM}}{\\sqrt{8\\ln 2}}.\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "\n",
    "5.  Achieving an effective $10'$ beam.\n",
    "If the input map has an (approximately Gaussian) effective FWHM $\\theta_{\\rm in}$\n",
    "and one wants an output effective FWHM $\\theta_{\\rm out}=10'$, apply an additional\n",
    "Gaussian smoothing with\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "\\theta_{\\rm add}=\\sqrt{\\theta_{\\rm out}^2-\\theta_{\\rm in}^2},\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "\\sigma_{\\rm add}=\\frac{\\theta_{\\rm add}}{\\sqrt{8\\ln 2}},\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "corresponding to\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "B_\\ell^{\\rm add}=\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{\\ell(\\ell+1)\\sigma_{\\rm add}^2}{2}\\right),\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "B_\\ell^{\\rm out}=B_\\ell^{\\rm in}\\,B_\\ell^{\\rm add}.\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "\n",
    "6.  Combined preprocessing formula.\n",
    "For each $X\\in\\{T,E,B\\}$, a harmonic-space ``smooth + downgrade'' step can be written as\n",
    "\\begin{equation}\n",
    "a_{\\ell m}^{X,{\\rm out}}=\n",
    "\\begin{cases}\n",
    "B_\\ell^{\\rm add}\\,a_{\\ell m}^{X,{\\rm in}}, & \\ell\\le \\ell_{\\max}^{\\rm out},\\\\\n",
    "0, & \\ell> \\ell_{\\max}^{\\rm out}.\n",
    "\\end{cases}\n",
    "\\end{equation}\n",
    "The final $(T,Q,U)$ maps at $N_{\\rm side}^{\\rm out}$ are obtained by synthesizing from\n",
    "$a_{\\ell m}^{T,{\\rm out}},a_{\\ell m}^{E,{\\rm out}},a_{\\ell m}^{B,{\\rm out}}$ and transforming\n",
    "back to Stokes parameters."
   ]
